  "contract": [
    "HR assembles native36-byte defaults with full sample rate at+4 and live channel count at+8; HRV uses24-byte defaults with rate at+4; SpO2 uses76-byte defaults with live channel count at+0 and rate at+4.",
    "Reuse actual C version builders and existing upstream HR/HRV/SpO2 configuration providers. Existing C default channel maps run in native order. Reject channels above4 HR or1 SpO2; propagate constructor results unchanged.",
    "Soft ADT clears its separate engine flag at20007c14, not the ADT flag array. Copy native60-byte defaults and replace only the low16-bit sample rate, preserving the packed upper halfword; ignore constructor return at its void boundary.",
    "NADT config/version and maximum channel getters supplied in C. Zero capacity for all interface-version getters deliberately preserves the native preceding-byte write; no new early-return guard."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Four context constructors remain modeled/unimplemented. Replacing four engine dependencies with these four lower-level constructors keeps application imports63 and boot imports22. This is progress through the call graph, not completed physical bring-up.",
    "All4080 direct comparisons pass with configuration bytes,20-byte interface records, full public channel maps and engine flag. Independent config/capacity/channel-limit oracles apply. All504 native entry instruction bytes execute. Actual C version/channel-map entry visits are counted.",
    "The2567-case chain executes actual C initialization controller, all adapters, engines, versions, interface getters and channel defaults. Controller/frame/init-state read/write traces match; channel maps and engine flag compare as final state and constructor snapshots. No exact channel-map write-width or interrupt-concurrency claim.",
    "Source cannot execute stock. Modeled constructors return through BX LR. Normal-return saved integer/FP registers, SP, masks and guards compare. Caller scratch, APSR, pointer numeric addresses for readonly getters and private stack scratch are excluded.",
    "The previously documented weights-version private overread difference remains; only terminated version text is consumed. No executable instruction arrays are included in C. Numeric NADT defaults match stock60 bytes exactly.",
    "The first full build rejected six duplicate configuration providers; those copies were removed and the existing providers reused. A negative fixture bookkeeping KeyError was repaired before all13 compiled defects were semantically rejected. Only the final clean build/corpora are admission evidence.",
    "One byte receives new native state ownership at20007c14. All869 previous nongenerated source/object pairs remain unchanged, and the tested object equals the normal880-unit build. Source-plan and cache layout remain unchanged; physical RAM/startup placement remains open.",
    "Final executable linking, context allocation/initialization, remaining hardware dependencies, physical sensor operation and boot remain open. Relocatable composition is not bootable firmware, and no instruction or image identity is claimed."
  ],
